# Godot 4 ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor caches and imported asset binaries. Never commit these; they are
# machine-specific and are the usual cause of Mac<->Windows churn.
.godot/
/android/

# Export artifacts. export_presets.cfg can contain machine-local output paths
# and signing details, so it stays out until we actually ship.
export_presets.cfg
/build/
/exports/
*.translation

# Local QA tools and logs. The portable Godot binary used by automated review is
# intentionally workspace-local and far too large (and too platform-specific)
# to belong in the project.
/.tools/
/.godot-*.log

# Scratch from asset generation. The finished portraits live in art/petitioners/;
# these are the pre-chroma-removal sources and alpha passes, ~12 MB of
# intermediates that nothing in the project loads.
/tmp/

# Godot editor data directories. These are created in the project folder as a
# side effect of running the editor with an explicit --path, and belong in the
# user's own editor data, not in the repository.
/export_templates/
/feature_profiles/
/script_templates/
/text_editor_themes/

# OS -----------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editors ------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# NOTE: *.uid files ARE committed on purpose. Godot 4.4+ writes a .gd.uid next to
# every script; if those are missing, the other machine generates different UIDs
# and every scene referencing a script shows as modified. Do not add them here.

# Scratch files left behind by review agents. They run probes against the real
# project to settle a claim, and a probe that gets committed is a probe that
# will one day be run. The encoding guard in tools/verify_content.py caught the
# first one; this stops the next.
tmp_*
